§ `Section 598 -- Election deemed to be waived`

-- (1), the BAR: JUST TRUE where the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury.
-- src:12722 | 598 (1) Notwithstanding anything in this Act, where a person to whom subsection 597(1) applies has elected or is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury and, at the time he failed to appear or to remain in attendance for his trial, he had not re-elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge without a jury, he shall not be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury unless
-- src:12723 | (a) he establishes to the satisfaction of a judge of the court in which he is indicted that there was a legitimate excuse for his failure to appear or remain in attendance for his trial; or
-- src:12724 | (b) the Attorney General requires pursuant to section 568 or 569 that the accused be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury.
@ref s 598(1) (src:12722-12724)
GIVEN `subsection 597(1) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has elected or is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the person failed to appear or to remain in attendance for the trial they had re-elected to be tried by a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person establishes to the satisfaction of a judge of the court in which they are indicted that there was a legitimate excuse for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General requires pursuant to section 568 or 569 that the accused be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 598(1) the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`subsection 597(1) applies to the person` AND `the person has elected or is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` AND (NOT `at the time the person failed to appear or to remain in attendance for the trial they had re-elected to be tried by a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge without a jury`)) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a person to whom subsection 597(1) applies has elected or is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury and, at the time he failed to appear or to remain in attendance for his trial, he had not re-elected" (the "where" of a bar fails: the subsection does not bar) [M-a]
        IF `the person establishes to the satisfaction of a judge of the court in which they are indicted that there was a legitimate excuse for the failure` OR `the Attorney General requires pursuant to section 568 or 569 that the accused be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he shall not be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury unless (a) he establishes to the satisfaction of a judge of the court in which he is indicted that there was a legitimate excuse" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12726 | (2) An accused who, under subsection (1), may not be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury is deemed to have elected under section 536 or 536.1 to be tried without a jury by a judge of the court where the accused was indicted and section 561 or 561.1, as the case may be, does not apply in respect of the accused.
@ref s 598(2) (src:12726-12726)
GIVEN `the answer of s 598(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 598(2) the accused is deemed to have elected to be tried without a jury by a judge, and section 561 or 561.1 does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 598(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who, under subsection (1), may not be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury"

§ `Section 599 -- Change of venue`

-- src:12730 | 599 (1) A court before which an accused is or may be indicted, at any term or sittings thereof, or a judge who may hold or sit in that court, may at any time before or after an indictment is found, on the application of the prosecutor or the accused, order the trial to be held in a territorial division in the same province other than that in which the offence would otherwise be tried if
-- src:12731 | (a) it appears expedient to the ends of justice, including
-- src:12732 | (i) to promote a fair and efficient trial, and
-- src:12733 | (ii) to ensure the safety and security of a victim or witness or to protect their interests and those of society; or
-- src:12734 | (b) a competent authority has directed that a jury is not to be summoned at the time appointed in a territorial division where the trial would otherwise by law be held.
@ref s 599(1) (src:12730-12734)
GIVEN `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other territorial division is in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears expedient to the ends of justice, including to promote a fair and efficient trial, or to ensure the safety and security of a victim or witness or to protect their interests and those of society` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a competent authority has directed that a jury is not to be summoned at the time appointed in the territorial division where the trial would otherwise by law be held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 599(1) the court or judge may order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the application of the prosecutor or the accused"
        IF NOT `the other territorial division is in the same province` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a territorial division in the same province other than that in which the offence would otherwise be tried"
        IF `it appears expedient to the ends of justice, including to promote a fair and efficient trial, or to ensure the safety and security of a victim or witness or to protect their interests and those of society` OR `a competent authority has directed that a jury is not to be summoned at the time appointed in the territorial division where the trial would otherwise by law be held` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if (a) it appears expedient to the ends of justice ...; or (b) a competent authority has directed that a jury is not to be summoned" [F:may-if]

