§ `Section 600 -- Order is authority to remove prisoner`

-- src:12743 | 600 An order that is made under section 599 is sufficient warrant, justification and authority to all sheriffs, keepers of prisons and peace officers for the removal, disposal and reception of an accused in accordance with the terms of the order, and the sheriff may appoint and authorize any peace officer to convey the accused to a prison in the territorial division in which the trial is ordered to be held.
@ref s 600 (src:12743-12743)
GIVEN `an order is made under section 599` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a sheriff, a keeper of a prison or a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the removal, disposal or reception of an accused in accordance with the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 600 the order is sufficient warrant, justification and authority for the act` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under section 599` AND `the person is a sheriff, a keeper of a prison or a peace officer` AND `the act is the removal, disposal or reception of an accused in accordance with the terms of the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to all sheriffs, keepers of prisons and peace officers for the removal, disposal and reception of an accused in accordance with the terms of the order"

